ids:Initial PCI IDs to add to the vfio driver, format is "vendor:device[:subvendor[:subdevice[:class[:class_mask]]]]" and multiple comma separated entries can be specified (string)
nointxmask:Disable support for PCI 2.3 style INTx masking.  If this resolves problems for specific devices, report lspci -vvvxxx to linux-pci@vger.kernel.org so the device can be fixed automatically via the broken_intx_masking flag. (bool)
disable_vga:Disable VGA resource access through vfio-pci (bool)
disable_idle_d3:Disable using the PCI D3 low power state for idle, unused devices (bool)
enable_sriov:Enable support for SR-IOV configuration.  Enabling SR-IOV on a PF typically requires support of the userspace PF driver, enabling VFs without such support may result in non-functional VFs or PF. (bool)
disable_denylist:Disable use of device denylist. Disabling the denylist allows binding to devices with known errata that may lead to exploitable stability or security issues when accessed by untrusted users. (bool)
allow_unsafe_interrupts:Enable VFIO IOMMU support for on platforms without interrupt remapping support. (bool)
disable_hugepages:Disable VFIO IOMMU support for IOMMU hugepages. (bool)
